tch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/f2a29faeb9db8e622a21a0e77bea911960a5c64d87a2c900ecd0c0213b2e4bce.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}.$" 13194139536166 true] [17592186096359 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/f2a29faeb9db8e622a21a0e77bea911960a5c64d87a2c900ecd0c0213b2e4bce.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}.$" 13194139536166 false] [17592186096476 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139536166 true] [17592186096476 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139536166 false] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386871 13194139536166 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386878 13194139536166 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386907 13194139536166 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386910 13194139536166 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386864 13194139536166 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386885 13194139536166 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386899 13194139536166 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386892 13194139536166 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386903 13194139536166 true] [17592186291643 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/1840ce2886aa3546371998239757a5dc500449007dc511dc0860b1ce59a59d2c.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown above." 13194139536166 true] [17592186291643 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/1840ce2886aa3546371998239757a5dc500449007dc511dc0860b1ce59a59d2c.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown above." 13194139536166 false] [17592186291657 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536166 true] [17592186291657 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536166 false] [17592186291698 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139536166 true] [17592186291698 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139536166 false] [17592186293424 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536166 true] [17592186293424 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536166 false] [17592186386864 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386865 13194139536166 true] [17592186386864 1089 "q-10031" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386864 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536166 true] [17592186386864 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/b77e20a705956f80379158fd88de70f95c94989c6bd7640d1f3c20d8cca7b4f5.png)\n\nFind the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above." 13194139536166 true] [17592186386864 1113 #uuid "271f1a42-87ca-513d-a0ea-447f94419077" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386864 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(1-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that we want to find the area between the curve $x=y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=1.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386866 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386867 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386868 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386869 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386870 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1041 "selection" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386868 13194139536166 true] [17592186386865 1110 #uuid "6cf63bd1-e91a-51c0-8b4a-f85a538e55bc" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386866 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536166 true] [17592186386866 1111 #uuid "2d1303ab-fd35-5148-b176-e4d68ff7bc9a" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386867 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536166 true] [17592186386867 1111 #uuid "d6ca3104-216d-55bc-8701-a2ddf6d07e77" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386868 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536166 true] [17592186386868 1111 #uuid "9fdd95aa-c3be-5c2c-a97b-b33317587384" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386869 1034 "1" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386869 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536166 true] [17592186386869 1111 #uuid "b9622dc1-4248-5603-ade0-5b3bba119aaf" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386870 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386870 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536166 true] [17592186386870 1111 #uuid "04104401-2fee-57f3-89af-b76539357e49" 13194139536166 true] [17592186386871 1017 #